From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nix-config integration <noreply@local>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cavemem: honor CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR env var in resolveDataDir

Written from scratch for the DWSR/nix-config cavemem integration; no
upstream PR exists. cavemem v0.2.1 (commit e934e43) hardcodes
`~/.cavemem` as the only data directory location: there is no flag,
no constructor arg, and no env var that an operator can use to point
cavemem at a different filesystem path. The home-manager module's
`home.cavemem.dataDir` option ends up as a no-op because the option
writes a value to settings.json but cavemem reads settings.json from
`~/.cavemem/settings.json` regardless, and even when settings.json IS
read its dataDir field is only consulted at runtime — there is no
override at the file-discovery layer.

Rather than touch every caller site (12+ call sites across the worker,
the mcp-server, the hooks runner, the embedding cache, and every CLI
command), this patch makes the existing `resolveDataDir(raw)` helper
in `packages/config/src/loader.ts` the single bottleneck: the env
var, when set and non-empty, takes precedence over the `raw` argument
that consumers pass in. Because every read/write path in cavemem
already routes through `resolveDataDir(settings.dataDir)` —
data.db, worker.pid, worker.state.json, models/, and settingsPath()
itself — adding the env-var check there propagates the override
everywhere automatically.

Affected file(s):  packages/config/src/loader.ts

Behavior:
- `CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR` set to a non-empty path → that path is used as
  the data dir for ALL cavemem state (settings.json, data.db,
  worker.pid, worker.state.json, models/).
- `CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR` unset, empty, or whitespace-only → fall back to
  the existing behavior (`~/.cavemem` default, or whatever
  `settings.dataDir` resolves to).
- Tilde expansion (`~/foo`) is NOT applied to the env var; the
  operator is expected to set an absolute path. The home-manager
  module wires a fully-resolved Nix-managed path so this is a
  non-issue in practice. Documenting it here so a future operator
  who sets the env var manually understands the limitation.

Re-application checklist for future cavemem version bumps:
- Confirm `packages/config/src/loader.ts` still defines
  `resolveDataDir(raw: string)` with the same signature; if upstream
  ever adds a parameter, accept it through the env-var fast path
  too.
- Confirm every consumer that opens cavemem state still routes
  through `resolveDataDir(settings.dataDir)` — grep the source
  tree for direct uses of `homedir()` or `'.cavemem'` and patch
  any new bypass introduced by upstream.
- Confirm `settingsPath(dataDir?)` still calls into
  `resolveDataDir(...)` (rather than computing the path inline) so
  the env var still overrides the settings.json discovery path.
- Re-run the smoke test: `nix build .#cavemem` succeeds,
  `grep -E "process\.env\.CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR"
  result/lib/node_modules/cavemem/dist/index.js` matches, and
  `CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR=/tmp/cm-test result/bin/cavemem status` reports
  the override path as the data dir.

Verified to apply cleanly with `git apply --check` against the v0.2.1
source tree (commit e934e436e0dcb68422475d85385f7f8eb5e449b1).
---
 packages/config/src/loader.ts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/config/src/loader.ts b/packages/config/src/loader.ts
index 02c7f8d..7a1b2c3 100644
--- a/packages/config/src/loader.ts
+++ b/packages/config/src/loader.ts
@@ -7,6 +7,13 @@ import { type Settings, SettingsSchema } from './schema.js';
 const DEFAULT_DIR = '.cavemem';
 
 export function resolveDataDir(raw: string): string {
+  // CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR env var, when set and non-empty, takes precedence over
+  // the caller's `raw` input (including the `settings.dataDir` value loaded
+  // from settings.json and the `~/.cavemem` default). Empty / whitespace-only
+  // values are treated as unset. Tilde expansion is NOT applied to the env
+  // var; operators are expected to pass an absolute path.
+  const env = process.env.CAVEMEM_DATA_DIR;
+  if (env && env.trim().length > 0) return resolve(env.trim());
   if (raw.startsWith('~')) return join(homedir(), raw.slice(1).replace(/^\/+/, ''));
   return resolve(raw);
 }
